WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.701
-Jurnee Smollett,
you look gorgeous!

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:04.367
-Oh, thank you!
-Thank you for being here!

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:06.267
-I'm so excited to
actually be in person.

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:09.701
-In person! We met on Zoom!
-Yeah, man.

00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:11.634
-Thank you for being here.
-You're alive. You're real.

00:00:11.634 --> 00:00:13.133
-Yeah, I'm a real person.
I'm a real boy.

00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:14.234
-He's real!

00:00:14.234 --> 00:00:15.267
-I've got a real beard
and everything.

00:00:15.267 --> 00:00:17.067
-Yeah, this is cool.
-I want to ask --

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:19.634
I know you just finished
filming with Jamie Fox?

00:00:19.634 --> 00:00:21.767
-Yeah.
-He's one of our friends.

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:23.868
He's just the greatest,
right? To work with.

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:25.467
-I mean, dream come true, man.

00:00:25.467 --> 00:00:27.634
-And fun, talented.
-Just so much fun.

00:00:27.634 --> 00:00:29.567
So generous as an actor,
you know?

00:00:29.567 --> 00:00:32.267
We did a film a few months ago
called "The Burial,"

00:00:32.267 --> 00:00:36.000
and we played litigators
and we played enemies.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.100
I play his adversary,
and I didn't meet him

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.834
until the day
we were supposed to shoot.

00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:44.701
Like, literally no rehearsal,
walk on set.

00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:46.000
You're like, alright.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.467
I'd been in the library
for months and courtrooms,

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:51.634
studying law and trying to
do all my research.

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:54.901
And he and I, we do this scene,
we go at it,

00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:57.167
And I'm thinking,
we're gonna be method.

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:59.100
He's gonna be my enemy, man.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.434
And then after
we finish the scene,

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:01.701
he comes up
and gives me a big hug.

00:01:01.701 --> 00:01:03.367
He's like,
"Jurnee, you killed it!"

00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:05.000
And I was like, Oh, my God.
-It makes you cry.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.234
You go, "I'm in love with you."
-I melted!

00:01:07.234 --> 00:01:09.267
I was like,
this guy is the coolest man.

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:10.634
-He's a charming man.

00:01:10.634 --> 00:01:13.267
-He's one of the greatest actors
of all time to me, so...

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:15.534
-I love him.
-"Django," right?

00:01:15.534 --> 00:01:17.200
-Come on. Everything.
He's unbelievable.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:18.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:22.501
-And also, you have
another co-star in that film,

00:01:22.501 --> 00:01:24.734
your five-year-old son, Hunter.

00:01:24.734 --> 00:01:26.334
How did that come about?

00:01:26.334 --> 00:01:30.100
-Our director, Maggie Betts,
called me, and she's like,

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.334
"Jurnee, we've auditioned
so many kids,

00:01:32.334 --> 00:01:35.501
and I just need a smart kid."

00:01:35.501 --> 00:01:36.968
And my son, Hunter --

00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:40.334
I know parents always think
their children are smart.

00:01:40.334 --> 00:01:44.467
However,
my son is five years old

00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:47.968
and he's reading and doing math
on the third grade level.

00:01:47.968 --> 00:01:50.701
-Wow.
-So he's really smart.

00:01:50.701 --> 00:01:52.567
And he wants to be
a paleontologist.

00:01:52.567 --> 00:01:54.667
He wants to bring the dinosaurs
back from extinction.

00:01:54.667 --> 00:01:56.367
-Oh, no way.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:56.367 --> 00:01:58.501
We're working on it.
-Hunter, do that, buddy.

00:01:58.501 --> 00:02:01.567
-Maggie is like, "Can Hunter
be in this scene with Jamie?"

00:02:01.567 --> 00:02:03.567
And I'm like, "Oh, I don't post
him on social media,

00:02:03.567 --> 00:02:07.467
but, you know, if he's ever
gonna do something in film,

00:02:07.467 --> 00:02:09.000
I mean, like...
-Put him in a movie.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.300
-With Jamie Foxx!
I mean, this is epic.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.667
You know? Like, he can do this.
-That's funny.

00:02:12.667 --> 00:02:16.834
-And so, he rehearses his
two lines for a month

00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:18.200
leading up to the scene, right?

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.934
He's like,
"I'm gonna be prepared."

00:02:19.934 --> 00:02:21.767
And we get there, I'm like,

00:02:21.767 --> 00:02:23.834
"Oh, my gosh, baby.
Look at the call sheet.

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:25.834
Your name is on the call sheet."

00:02:25.834 --> 00:02:27.667
He looks at it and he goes,

00:02:27.667 --> 00:02:29.767
"Why am I number 67?"

00:02:29.767 --> 00:02:31.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.434 --> 00:02:33.501
I snatch the call sheet from him

00:02:33.501 --> 00:02:36.601
and he's like,
"Well, who's number one?"

00:02:36.601 --> 00:02:39.801
I say,
"Jamie Foxx, Oscar winner."

00:02:39.801 --> 00:02:41.400
And he says,
"Well, who's number two?"

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:45.334
And I say, "Tommy Lee Jones.
You know, legend, icon."

00:02:45.334 --> 00:02:47.133
And he says,
"Well, who's number three?"

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:50.067
And I say,
"Mommy is number three."

00:02:50.067 --> 00:02:51.601
And he looks at me
and he's like,

00:02:51.601 --> 00:02:54.601
"So I'm number 67, and
you're number three?"

00:02:54.601 --> 00:02:57.100
-No! Whoa.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:58.868
-I was like, "Kid...

00:02:58.868 --> 00:03:02.267
you're never, ever acting,
ever again."

00:03:02.267 --> 00:03:04.467
Like, stick with
the paleontology.

00:03:04.467 --> 00:03:07.267
-I know you star in films,

00:03:07.267 --> 00:03:09.100
but this is your first movie
that you're starring in

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.601
and executive producing.

00:03:10.601 --> 00:03:11.801
-Yeah.
-This is a big deal.

00:03:11.801 --> 00:03:13.734
"Lou." Congratulations on that.
-Thank you.

00:03:13.734 --> 00:03:15.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.434
-How did you get involved
with this now?

00:03:16.434 --> 00:03:17.934
Allison Janney?

00:03:17.934 --> 00:03:20.434
-Yeah, Allison Janney,
she's such an icon.

00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:23.133
At 61 years old --
you guys gotta see this film.

00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:26.234
She's kicking butt,
doing all her own stunts.

00:03:26.234 --> 00:03:28.300
It's really amazing.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:30.601
It's produced by J.J. Abrams
and Bad Robot,

00:03:30.601 --> 00:03:33.200
and it's a fun film, you know?

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.267
It's an intense thriller

00:03:35.267 --> 00:03:39.133
in which two women have to
go on this rescue mission

00:03:39.133 --> 00:03:41.601
to rescue a little girl
who's been kidnapped,

00:03:41.601 --> 00:03:42.901
my character's daughter.

00:03:42.901 --> 00:03:45.400
And we come from very
different backgrounds

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:47.234
and are forced to work together
even though

00:03:47.234 --> 00:03:49.434
we kind of hate each other.
-Yeah.

00:03:49.434 --> 00:03:51.067
And while you're filming this,

00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:53.801
you get the news that you were
nominated for an Emmy.

00:03:53.801 --> 00:03:55.734
-Yeah.
-Wow, this is cool,

00:03:55.734 --> 00:03:57.033
that' everything's
happening right now.

00:03:57.033 --> 00:04:00.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:00.133 --> 00:04:03.167
-And after you find out you're
getting nominated and you go,

00:04:03.167 --> 00:04:04.701
"Oh, my gosh,
I'm so excited I got nominated,

00:04:04.701 --> 00:04:05.901
this is awesome,"

00:04:05.901 --> 00:04:07.801
Allison Janney
gets nominated for an Emmy.

00:04:07.801 --> 00:04:10.534
The same day!
-I know, but she didn't know.

00:04:10.534 --> 00:04:13.300
I'm in the makeup trailer
and I get the call.

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:14.467
I'm screaming.

00:04:14.467 --> 00:04:15.567
It's my first time being
nominated for an Emmy.

00:04:15.567 --> 00:04:16.901
-Of course.

00:04:16.901 --> 00:04:18.133
-She comes over and she's like,
"What's the matter?"

00:04:18.133 --> 00:04:20.000
And I'm like,
"I got nominated for an Emmy!"

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:23.100
She's like, "Hell yeah, you did.
I voted for you."

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.434
-That's what friends are for.
-Yeah!

00:04:24.434 --> 00:04:26.634
I run out of the trailer.
I call my family.

00:04:26.634 --> 00:04:28.167
My brother tells me,
"You know, your co-star

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:29.400
got nominated as well."

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.367
I was like, "I was just
in the trailer with her!"

00:04:31.367 --> 00:04:32.901
And so I go on set
to rehearse,

00:04:32.901 --> 00:04:34.100
and I'm like, "Congratulations!"

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:35.467
She says, "For what?"

00:04:35.467 --> 00:04:36.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.701 --> 00:04:39.367
I was like,
"You got nominated for 'Mom.'"

00:04:39.367 --> 00:04:41.901
And she's like,
"Shut up, shut up. No way."

00:04:41.901 --> 00:04:43.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.000
-You're like,
"Let's just party! Let's go!"

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:48.033
-Dude, it's like,
her 17th nomination.

00:04:48.033 --> 00:04:49.801
-She's a legend.
-It was my first, so, you know.

00:04:49.801 --> 00:04:51.501
-Yeah, come on.
-She's such a legend.

00:04:51.501 --> 00:04:52.968
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:52.968 --> 00:04:55.901
Here's Jurnee Smollett
and Allison Janney in "Lou."

00:04:55.901 --> 00:04:56.934
Take a look at this.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:59.634
-Her father took her.
-Her father?

00:04:59.634 --> 00:05:03.167
-Uh-huh. He's -- He's here.
How the hell is he here?

00:05:03.167 --> 00:05:05.100
-Hold on, you saw him?

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:07.901
-No, I -- He --

00:05:07.901 --> 00:05:10.267
He's supposed to be dead,
but he found us.

00:05:10.267 --> 00:05:11.901
I thought -- I thought
we were free of him.

00:05:11.901 --> 00:05:15.300
He killed Chris.
-Jesus Christ.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:18.000
-Where are your keys?
My car won't start.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.200
I've got to get to the sheriff.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:20.300
-I'll drive.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:22.033
[ Keys jingling ]

00:05:22.033 --> 00:05:23.534
[ Thunder cracks ]

00:05:23.534 --> 00:05:26.934
[ Engine sputters ]

00:05:27.667 --> 00:05:28.901
-Hmm.

00:05:28.901 --> 00:05:32.434
[ Engine splutters ]
-Come on, come on.

00:05:32.434 --> 00:05:34.701
[ Thunder cracks ]

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:38.634
♪♪

00:05:38.634 --> 00:05:42.834
[ Children's melody playing ]

00:05:42.834 --> 00:05:44.133
-What's wrong?
-Run!

00:05:44.133 --> 00:05:45.701
-Whoa!

00:05:45.701 --> 00:05:47.133
[ Applause ]

00:05:47.133 --> 00:05:49.000
-Jurnee Smollett, everyone!

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:51.300
"Lou" is streaming now
on Netflix.

